---
title: Carrot Cake III
cookTime: 30 mins
source.name: Allrecipes.com
source.url: http://allrecipes.com/Recipe/Carrot-Cake-III/Detail.aspx?src=etaf
tags: Desserts
---

= Cake =
Preheat oven to 350°F.
@Oil and @flour a #9x13 inch pan{}.

In a #large bowl{}, beat together @eggs{4}, @vegetable oil{1 1/4%cups}, @white sugar{2%cups} and @vanilla extract{2%tsp}.

Mix in @all-purpose flour{2%cups}, @baking soda{2%tsp}, @baking powder{2%tsp}, @salt{1/2%tsp} and @ground cinnamon{2%tsp}.

Stir in @carrots{3%cups}(grated). Fold in @pecans{1%cup}(chopped).
Pour into prepared pan.

Bake in the preheated oven for ~{40-50%minutes}, or until a toothpick inserted into the center of the cake comes out clean.
Let cool in pan for ~{10%minutes}, then turn out onto a wire rack and cool completely.

= Frosting =
To Make Frosting: In a medium bowl, combine @butter{1/2%cup}(softened), @cream cheese{8%oz}(softened),
@powdered sugar{4%cups}, and @vanilla extract{1%tsp}. 
Beat until the mixture is smooth and creamy. 

Stir in @pecans{1%cup}(chopped). Frost the cooled cake.
